## Phase 3 — Intake / 2026-08-29 / Commit: c034770 ("phase 3: intake, entropy, safety, location, simulator") + tests (uncommitted)

### Built

Domain — `src/domain/`, all pure, no I/O, no clock, no `Math.random`:
- `faults.ts` — 12 `FAULT_CODES`, `FAULT_PRIORS` (base rates), and
  `CAPABILITIES_BY_FAULT` mapping each fault to the technician capability that
  resolves it. Capability codes match `prisma/seed/capabilities.ts`.
- `symptoms.ts` — `symptomPayloadSchema` (Zod): `primaryComplaint`,
  `engineCranks`, `warningLights[]`, `unusualSound`, `vehicleMoves`. The INPUT
  boundary Phase 16 will re-source from free text.
- `faultRules.ts` — the hand-written naive-Bayes table. `classifySymptoms()`
  folds `COMPLAINT_LIKELIHOOD`, `ENGINE_CRANKS_LIKELIHOOD`,
  `WARNING_LIGHT_LIKELIHOOD`, `SOUND_LIKELIHOOD`, `VEHICLE_MOVES_LIKELIHOOD`
  into the priors in a fixed order. Also exports `symptomLikelihood()` — the
  same table read generatively, for the simulator.
- `entropy.ts` — `shannonEntropy`, `normalise`, `applyLikelihood`, `rankFaults`,
  `topFault`.
- `questions.ts` — `INTAKE_QUESTIONS`, 7 questions with P(answer | fault) rows;
  `answerLikelihood()` returns a UNIFORM row for a fault a question does not
  model.
- `questionSelection.ts` — `expectedInformationGain`, `expectedPosteriorEntropy`,
  `posteriorForAnswer`, `selectNextQuestion`, `stopReasonFor`,
  `decideNextQuestion`. Constants: `ENTROPY_STOP_THRESHOLD_BITS = 0.65`,
  `MAX_QUESTIONS = 5`, `MIN_EXPECTED_GAIN_BITS = 0.02`.
- `capabilitySet.ts` — `contendingFaults` (80% coverage mass, max 3),
  `requiredCapabilities`, `capabilitySetIsStable`.
- `safety.ts` — `safetyContextSchema`, 9 rules in `SAFETY_RULES`,
